id     = "slider-drag"
about  = """A volume slider bound both ways (`value: <-> vol`) is dragged right,
then quickly left past its start, then set from outside, with a meter of
the same value beside it (spec.md 8.5: a slider dragged writes its
target; decisions.md 2026-10-06 "only two-way values move": a drag and
the drawing share one span, so the knob stays under the pointer). While
it is held, the knob and the filled part of the track are under the
pointer each frame:
the drag writes the value and the slider draws it at once, never a frame
behind. A value set from outside springs the knob and the fill, and the
meter springs after it. The knob's and the fill's places in the slider
are its parts in the trace (`pt`, docs/eval.md "Paint"). Held-out set
D's slider-lag drew the knob one frame behind the pointer."""
screen = { width = 300, scale = 1.0 }

=== shell.strand
state vol = 0.3

bar Top {
  height: 30; bg: #1e1e2e
  row { height: 24; gap: 8; align: center
    slider { id: knob; width: 120; value: <-> vol }
    meter vol { id: level; width: 100; height: 6; color: #89b4fa; track: #313244 }
  }
}

=== steps
rest
mark drag
drag 39,12 -> 91,12 over 400
rest
mark drag-back
drag 91,12 -> 20,12 over 250
rest
mark external
set vol 0.6
rest
